      "created_at": "2025-12-13T04:35:08Z",
      "updated_at": "2025-12-13T04:35:08Z",
      "body": "My setup is more messy than OP's. I am running in Kubernetes with five Vulkan (Vega 10 GPU) workers with the v3.8.0-gpu-vulkan container image and one pod with plain v3.8.0 as the API server. However, I am seeing the same symptom as @lvnvpreet.\n\nPer @Expro's research in #3968, I strongly agree the change in llama.cpp is responsible: https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/898acba6816ad23b6a9491347d30e7570bffadfd \n\nPresumably the code in https://github.com/mudler/LocalAI/blob/2bd6faaff5281ca6c461b9c000b83a35ffc723dc/backend/cpp/llama-cpp/grpc-server.cpp#L331 needs an update. Maybe this weekend will be the weekend I successfully build LocalAI \ud83d\ude42 \n\nAs a workaround, I have pinned all of my LocalAI pods to use v3.6.0 of the backend using [this gist](https://gist.github.com/sredman/d5667f31e763fdf4fa218907c36fd000) as a [custom gallery](https://localai.io/backends/index.html#adding-a-backend-gallery), and my distributed inference is working correctly. AFAICT, v3.6.0 was released just before the change mentioned above.",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
